{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use existing performance test framework for U1 to run baseline, Tuple, and Serialized payloads against Kafka 0.8.1 and 0.8.2.",
    "Upgrade Reactor dependency to 2.0.3 in Gradle build files for U2, and address any API changes in the codebase.",
    "Modify Spring configuration files (e.g., XML or Java config) to disable JMX by default for U3, while providing a property to enable it.",
    "Fix Gradle build scripts (build.gradle, settings.gradle) to resolve dist and distZip task failures for U4.",
    "Enable compiler and javadoc warning flags in the build configuration for U5, then systematically fix warnings across modules.",
    "Update RPM spec files and init scripts to support multiple xd-container instances via separate configuration directories and PID files for U6.",
    "Restructure documentation (likely AsciiDoc) to add cross-references and navigation for OOTB batch jobs (U7) and analytics tab widgets (U8)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Performance test environment with Kafka 0.8.1 and 0.8.2 is available and can be provisioned within the estimated time.",
    "Reactor 2.0.3 upgrade does not require major architectural changes; only API adaptations in XD code.",
    "JMX is currently enabled by default in a central configuration location, making it straightforward to flip the default.",
    "Build issues are isolated to the dist and distZip Gradle tasks and do not indicate deeper dependency problems.",
    "Compiler and javadoc warnings are fixable with localized code changes and do not require large-scale refactoring.",
    "RPM packaging follows standard practices and can be extended with instance-specific configuration without redesign.",
    "Documentation source is in a structured format (e.g., AsciiDoc) that allows easy linking and reorganization.",
    "All changes are confined to the Spring XD project; no modifications to Spring Framework core are needed."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.1",
      "activity_name": "Set up performance test environment",
      "activity_description": "Provision and configure test environment with Kafka 0.8.1 and 0.8.2, including required sinks (In-Memory Transport > Hdfs sink, Direct Binding Transport > Hdfs Sink, Kafka > Hdfs Sink).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1.2",
      "activity_name": "Update performance test scripts",
